From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: follow the Mac input source and its Caps Lock switch

Applies after the Try Omarchy Cocoa input patches.

On a Mac with a Korean input source, Caps Lock is the 한/영 key: a short
press switches the input source and a long press locks capitals. Before
this patch a short press reached the guest as nothing, and holding Caps
Lock with the VM focused could not lock capitals on the Mac.

macOS does not document how it reports this, so the patch follows what
it was measured to do. A short press arrives only through the HID event
tap, as a flagsChanged event with keyCode 0xff that AppKit drops before
-sendEvent:. While the key is down, macOS locks Caps Lock provisionally
and undoes it for a short press, so every Caps Lock state seen during
the press flickers. A long press is confirmed by a 0xff event that is
flagged and locked, and moves the Mac to ABC.

When the launcher sets TRYOMARCHY_CAPS_LOCK=hangul (Korean is the Mac's
only non-Latin input method) or input-method (others are enabled):

- The full-grab tap handles the kVK_CapsLock and 0xff events and passes
  them on, and -sendEvent: hands them to AppKit, handling them in QEMU
  only when the tap is not capturing. Consuming them kept macOS from
  locking capitals.
- The guest's input method follows the Mac input source with absolute
  keys: Henkan when the Mac's source is an input mode that cannot type
  ASCII, Muhenkan otherwise. Omarchy's Fcitx profile already uses them to
  activate and deactivate the input method. They are sent at the selected
  input source notification while the VM window is key and at the next
  key after it becomes key. In hangul mode they are sent again before a
  space, return, tab, escape or arrow key every two seconds. Fcitx passes
  a redundant Henkan on to the engine, so the repeat waits for a key that
  ends a Hangul syllable anyway. A toggle could not be kept right: Fcitx
  keeps a state per window, a lone Shift also toggles it, and a switch
  sent before Fcitx runs at boot is lost. Other input methods get no
  repeat: a lone Shift leaves Pinyin for a moment, and Henkan converts in
  Mozc.
- The full-grab tap passes on the Globe action event (keyCode 0xb3), so
  Globe switches the Mac input source with the VM focused, and the guest
  follows.
- Events from the Caps Lock key never sync the guest's Caps Lock. Key
  and modifier events sync it from the IOHIDSystem lock state, compared
  with the Caps Lock light the guest reports through virtio-input, once
  the press is decided: the lock state reads unlocked, a long press is
  confirmed, or a second passes.

Missing or other values change nothing.

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
